   },
   {
    "quote": "Entity resolution is the single most analytically intensive step in most OSINT investigations — it requires systematic methodology, tolerance for ambiguity, and rigorous evidence documentation to avoid misidentification. Misidentification is not merely an analytical failure; in intelligence and legal contexts it is an operational and ethical risk that can cause concrete harm to innocent parties.",
    "url": "https://intelligencenotes.com/08-Guides--and--Manuals/OSINT-Methodologies/Entity-Resolution-Methodology",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-07"
